{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "suite": "load",
  "about": "What `require` of each public entry costs a fresh Node process, as a CommonJS host loads it, before any call into it. Each row adds to `node`, the harness alone; an entry's row includes the packages it pulls in, so rows overlap and don't add up. Rows past the SDK's own packages come from each pack's config, resolved from that pack's directory; a pack bundled from source excludes what transpiling it would cost. `CJS modules` counts entries in `require.cache`; a CommonJS entry that loads ES modules adds modules it doesn't count.",
